        },
        "cap": "A girl waters a drooping flower, which perks up and sparkles."
      },
      {
        "t": "key",
        "html": "<b>re-</b> = <b>back, again</b>. <b>de-</b> = <b>down, away, from</b>; sometimes <b>completely</b>."
      },
      {
        "t": "p",
        "html": "These two are among the most common prefixes in English: twenty words on the list start with <i>re-</i> and sixteen with <i>de-</i>. Many <i>de-</i> words describe putting someone down: <i>deride</i> (laugh down at), <i>denigrate</i> (blacken), <i>denounce</i> (speak against)."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "The parts and their words"
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-roots",
        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "root": "re",
          "words": [
            "revive",
            "rejuvenate",
            "recurrent",
            "reclusive",
            "relinquish",
            "reticent",
            "retrospect",
            "renounce",
            "revere",
            "repress"
          ]
        },
        "cap": "Words on the list built on re- (back, again)."
      },
      {
        "t": "viz",
        "name": "vo-roots",
        "opts": {
          "max": 10,
          "root": "de",
          "words": [
            "dejected",
            "deduce",
            "denigrate",
            "deride",
            "demolish",
            "despondent",
            "deter",
            "devastate",
            "denounce",
            "decadent"
          ]
        },
        "cap": "Words on the list built on de- (down, away, completely)."
      },
      {
        "t": "h",
        "text": "Words taken apart"
      },
      {
        "t": "table",
        "head": [
          "Word and meaning",
          "Parts, and what they say"
        ],
        "rows": [
          [
            "<b>revive</b><br>to bring back to life or use",
            "<b>re-</b> <i>again</i> + viv <i>live</i> + -e<br>→ “live again”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>rejuvenate</b><br>to make young or fresh again",
            "<b>re-</b> <i>again</i> + juven <i>young</i> + -ate<br>→ “make young again”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>recurrent</b><br>happening again and again",
            "<b>re-</b> <i>back, again</i> + curr <i>run</i> + -ent<br>→ “running back again”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>reclusive</b><br>avoiding the company of others",
            "<b>re-</b> <i>away</i> + clus <i>shut</i> + -ive<br>→ “shut away”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>relinquish</b><br>to give up",
            "<b>re-</b> <i>behind</i> + linqu <i>leave</i> + -ish<br>→ “leave behind”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>dejected</b><br>sad and discouraged",
            "<b>de-</b> <i>down</i> + ject <i>throw</i> + -ed<br>→ “thrown down”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>deduce</b><br>to reach a conclusion by reasoning",
            "<b>de-</b> <i>from</i> + duc <i>lead</i> + -e<br>→ “lead from (the facts)”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>denigrate</b><br>to criticize unfairly; to belittle",
            "<b>de-</b> <i>completely</i> + nigr <i>black</i> + -ate<br>→ “blacken”"
          ],
          [
            "<b>deride</b><br>to mock and make fun of",
            "<b>de-</b> <i>down</i> + rid <i>laugh</i> + -e<br>→ “laugh down at”"
          ]
        ],
        "cap": "Each word, what it means now, and its parts."
      },
      {
        "t": "ex",
        "title": "Use the parts",
        "q": "Usually chatty, Rosa was <b>reticent</b> about her plans and would say nothing. What does <i>reticent</i> mean?",
        "steps": [
          "Take it apart: <b>re-</b> (back) + <b>tic</b> (be silent, from Latin <i>tacere</i>, as in <i>tacit</i>) + <b>-ent</b>.",
          "Literally: “keeping silent back,” holding words back.",
          "The sentence fits: she would say nothing."
        ],
        "a": "Not revealing one’s thoughts or feelings readily."
      },
